IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gas-consumer`

-- Gas Act 2001, ss 2, 6, 11-13, 22, 29-32B, 39, 44, 46, 47, 49, 50, 52-60, 64, 89, 91, 92 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_gas-act-2001_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `fixtures`

`my flat on piped natural gas` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `the kind of gas` IS `piped natural gas`
    `gas is shipped to my premises` IS FALSE
    `my premises are connected to a gas pipeline network to get gas` IS TRUE

`my kitchen on an LPG cylinder` MEANS `My supply` WITH
    `the kind of gas` IS `liquefied petroleum gas`
    `gas is shipped to my premises` IS FALSE
    `my premises are connected to a gas pipeline network to get gas` IS FALSE

`me reselling retailed gas to my tenants` MEANS `My activity` WITH
    `what I do` IS `reselling retailed gas for use in premises I have an interest in`
    `the Minister's gazetted date has passed` IS FALSE
    `I hold a gas licence for it` IS FALSE
    `I am exempted under section 8` IS FALSE

`me retailing gas before the Minister's date` MEANS `My activity` WITH
    `what I do` IS `retailing gas`
    `the Minister's gazetted date has passed` IS FALSE
    `I hold a gas licence for it` IS FALSE
    `I am exempted under section 8` IS FALSE

`me retailing gas after the Minister's date` MEANS `My activity` WITH
    `what I do` IS `retailing gas`
    `the Minister's gazetted date has passed` IS TRUE
    `I hold a gas licence for it` IS FALSE
    `I am exempted under section 8` IS FALSE

`me piping gas to my neighbour's premises unlicensed` MEANS `My activity` WITH
